{"role":"assistant","content":"Fixed. The problem and the change:\n\n**Root cause** — `build_system()` in bot.py sent the whole prompt (instructions + athlete tail) as one block with a single `cache_control` marker. Prefix-hash caching means one changed byte evicts everything, so every `save_fact` forced a full ~1000-token re-creation — the `cache_creation ≈ full prompt, cache_read = 0` pattern on lines 5, 10, 14, 16, 23, 29 of logs/usage.jsonl.\n\n**Fix** (bot.py:130) — the system prompt is now two blocks, each with its own `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}` marker:\n1. The `INSTRUCTIONS` constant (byte-stable — nothing interpolated into it)\n2. `athlete_context(...)` — date, profile, zones, goal, facts, language\n\nThe rendered text is byte-identical to before; nothing else was touched. After a memory write, only the tail re-caches; the instructions stay hot.\n\n**Verified offline** (no API key here, so no live call): compiles, imports without the SDK, and a simulation of Anthropic's prefix-hash caching confirms the static chunk is unchanged by a simulated `save_fact` and across different users/dates, while the tail chunk changes. Expected log signature after deploy: post-`save_fact` calls show `cache_read` covering the instructions and `cache_creation` ≈ tail size only.\n\nANSWER.md records all of this, including which parts of your colleague's note applied (the two-segment fix, leaving keyword tool filtering alone, the existing usage logging, and the \"inject all facts, no top-N selection\" rule already being satisfied) and which were just their numbers. One pre-existing quirk I left alone per NOTES.md: pulling in an extra tool group mid-chat still re-creates the whole cache once (tools sit above the system prompt in the prefix) — visible at usage.jsonl line 26, and the note explicitly calls that liveable."}
